        <groundspeak:log id="684645555">
          <groundspeak:log_wpt lat="53.556000" lon="-113.391750" />
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="11091667">WillowZilla</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP751 - Rundle Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I DNF'd this one back in the winter when we found the other Rundle Park one.  I can see why now, the layer of snow over the area we tried kicking around would have filled the 3-4&quot; deep hole this one is stuck in.  Super Easy to spot today due to that same hole.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684649324">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="946600">Black Shark</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP751 Rundle Park&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rather than make the long drive around from Rundle Park into the residential area for this cap we parked in a second parking lot in the Park and walked up the hill.  We managed to walk across the frisbee golf course between groups without becoming a course hazard.  After a quick find we turned to appreciate the view which included many summer activities being enjoyed, industrial works and a good look at the black clouds first noticed at the cap below.  Those would be the late afternoon showers that were forecast.  Hopefully, they would be tardy as we had more caps to find!  Thanks for the cap and the view.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684211785">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="7458582">mkPerry</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP751 Rundle Park

Out again this evening to get a few more BCPs. We drove through a torrential downpour on the way here. Was a quick find after parking. We lucked out that the rain held off. After a couple quick pics on to the next one. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks outforthehunt for all the BCPs and the fun I've had over the last couple weeks getting most of the ones in the Edmonton area. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
